menu "OpenShock"

# The board's GPIO assignments deliberately do NOT live here.
#
# A Kconfig symbol ends up in sdkconfig.h, which most of ESP-IDF includes, so two
# boards that differed only by an LED pin produced a different sdkconfig.h and
# therefore shared no compiled framework objects at all. The pins are stamped into
# the image per board instead (BoardDescriptor.h): bare `OPENSHOCK_*=` lines in
# boards/<board>.defaults, stripped from the sdkconfig fragment by scripts/build.py.
#
# Everything in it is identical across every board and build channel, so it costs
# nothing in shared objects. Keep it that way: a setting that has to differ per
# board or per channel doesn't belong here (see OPENSHOCK_LOG_LEVEL_CHOICE).
#
# Fixed in code on purpose: the RF protocol timings, the E-Stop debounce, hold and
# rearm times (safety behaviour), task core affinity, and on-flash formats.
#
# Each component keeps its own settings in components/<name>/Kconfig.openshock. They are
# all sourced here, also for components a build leaves out, so every CONFIG_OPENSHOCK_*
# symbol exists in every build (the host tests build only their own sources).

orsource "../components/*/Kconfig.openshock"

endmenu
